{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0321","billNumberShort":"H.B. 321","billNumberLong":"HB0321S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0412","shortTitle":"Inmate Medical Treatment Rates Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"FIEFID","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Fiefia, Doug","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses medical treatment rates for inmates.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>creates a restricted account known as the Inmate Medical Treatment Restricted Account (restricted account);<hr><ltbullet>requires the Department of Health and Human Services (department) to pay the University of Utah Hospitals and Clinics and the University of Utah's physician groups Medicare rates for medical services rendered to inmates;<hr><ltbullet>requires the department to submit a report to the Health and Human Services Interim Committee and the Law Enforcement and Criminal Justice Interim Committee that includes:<hr><ltbullet1>a calculation of savings from paying the Medicare rate; and<hr><ltbullet1>an accounting of the restricted account;<hr><ltbullet>defines terms; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Amy Shewan","fiscalAnalyst":"Kevin Edminster","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"OGUGFXAUOB","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 08:59:14.200","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 08:59:14.200","actionClass":"L","v